 217:PhysPlateReverb.cpp **** /* ========================================================================
 218:PhysPlateReverb.cpp ****  * SECTION 2 — Temporary Work Buffers (only used during Init)
 219:PhysPlateReverb.cpp ****  *
 220:PhysPlateReverb.cpp ****  * These live in external SDRAM (64 MB) via the DSY_SDRAM_BSS attribute.
 221:PhysPlateReverb.cpp ****  * In MATLAB all these would just be regular workspace variables; in C++
 222:PhysPlateReverb.cpp ****  * on the Daisy we manually choose where big arrays go.
 223:PhysPlateReverb.cpp ****  *
 224:PhysPlateReverb.cpp ****  * DSY_SDRAM_BSS tells the linker: "put this in the .sdram_bss section"
 225:PhysPlateReverb.cpp ****  * which maps to the external 64 MB SDRAM chip, not the smaller internal
 226:PhysPlateReverb.cpp ****  * SRAM (≈512 KB).  The arrays persist after Init() but that's fine —
 227:PhysPlateReverb.cpp ****  * SDRAM has plenty of room.
 228:PhysPlateReverb.cpp ****  * ========================================================================*/
 229:PhysPlateReverb.cpp **** 
 230:PhysPlateReverb.cpp **** /* MATLAB equivalents:
 231:PhysPlateReverb.cpp ****  *   omega          → raw_omega[]     (modal angular frequencies)
