 249:PhysPlateReverb.cpp **** /* ========================================================================
 250:PhysPlateReverb.cpp ****  * SECTION 3 — ModalPlateReverb Class
 251:PhysPlateReverb.cpp ****  *
 252:PhysPlateReverb.cpp ****  * This class encapsulates the entire physical model.  It owns:
 253:PhysPlateReverb.cpp ****  *   • the pruned modal parameter arrays (ω, β², φ_i, φ_o)
 254:PhysPlateReverb.cpp ****  *   • the state-update coefficient arrays (B, C, D)
 255:PhysPlateReverb.cpp ****  *   • the state vectors (p1, p2) that persist between samples
 256:PhysPlateReverb.cpp ****  *
 257:PhysPlateReverb.cpp ****  * In MATLAB these are all separate workspace variables.  Wrapping them
 258:PhysPlateReverb.cpp ****  * in a C++ class keeps everything organized and avoids name collisions.
 259:PhysPlateReverb.cpp ****  * ========================================================================*/
 260:PhysPlateReverb.cpp **** class ModalPlateReverb
 261:PhysPlateReverb.cpp **** {
 262:PhysPlateReverb.cpp **** public:
 263:PhysPlateReverb.cpp ****     /* -------------------------------------------------------------------
 264:PhysPlateReverb.cpp ****      * Init()
